---
description: Do not pass QueryClient into helpers. Seed the cache at the page, layout, or hook call site.
alwaysApply: true
---

# QueryClient Call Site

`QueryClient` is owned where the request or event runs. Do not thread it into `api`, `lib`, `services`, or other helpers.

## Do

```ts
const queryClient = getQueryClient();
const result = await loadBoardInfoListResult();
if (result.ok) {
  queryClient.setQueryData(boardQueries.list().queryKey, result.data);
}
```

Client hooks use `useQueryClient()` in that hook, then `setQueryData` / `invalidateQueries` there.

## Do Not

```ts
export async function hydrateBoardInfoListQuery(queryClient: QueryClient) {
  const result = await loadBoardInfoListResult();
  if (result.ok) {
    queryClient.setQueryData(boardQueries.list().queryKey, result.data);
  }
  return result;
}
```

```ts
export function recoverOnlineQueries(queryClient: QueryClient) {
  await queryClient.invalidateQueries();
}
```

## Allowed

- `getQueryClient` / `makeQueryClient` factories
- Test wrappers that take `QueryClient` to build `QueryClientProvider`
- Direct `queryClient.*` in the same page, layout, hook, or socket handler that created the client
